  "description_html": "Size comparison of the titanosaurian sauropod <i>Petrobrasaurus puestohernandezi</i>, which was approximately 18 metres (59 ft) long. The sauropod is based on Filippi et. al. (2011) and <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.skeletaldrawing.com/sauropods-and-kin/futalognkosaurus\">Scott Hartman's <i>Futalognkosaurus</i> skeletal</a>. The human silhouette 180 cm is from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silhouette_of_man_standing_and_facing_forward.svg\" title=\"File:Silhouette of man standing and facing forward.svg\">File:Silhouette of man standing and facing forward.svg</a> (CC0).\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ul><li><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Filippi, Leonardo S.; Canudo, José Ignacio; Salgado, Leonardo J.; Garrido, Alberto C.; Garcia, Rodolfo A.; Cerda, Ignacio A.; Otero, Alejandro (2011). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Jose_Canudo/publication/235586462_A_new_sauropod_titanosaur_from_the_Plottier_Formation_Upper_Cretaceous_of_Patagonia_Argentina/links/09e41511d674e7d428000000.pdf\">A new sauropod titanosaur from the Plottier Formation (Upper Cretaceous) of Patagonia (Argentina)</a>\". <i>Geologica Acta</i> <b>9</b> (1): 1–12. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1344/105.000001648\">10.1344/105.000001648</a>.</cite></li>\n<li>Holtz, T. (2012). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.geol.umd.edu/~tholtz/dinoappendix/HoltzappendixWinter2011.pdf\">Genus List for Holtz (2008): Dinosaurs</a>.</li></ul>",
